        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: evil clown, comic clown, horror elements, dark humor\n- People: Stephen King\n- Products: It\n- Topics: horror fiction archetypes\n\nFacts:\n- The evil clown is a subversion of the traditional comic clown character.\n- The evil clown trope makes a playful clown disturbing through horror elements and dark humor.\n- In 1986, Stephen King published It, a horror novel.\n- It was Stephen King's 22nd book and his 18th novel published under his own name.\n- It popularized the modern archetype of the evil clown.\n- It follows seven children who are terrorized by a being that exploits victims' fears and phobias to disguise itself while hunting them.",
